WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.452
There are two companion files for this module.

00:00:02.452 --> 00:00:02.832
The first is the sample knowledge base, stored as a CSV file.

00:00:02.832 --> 00:00:05.122
It contains the source documents and metadata.

00:00:05.122 --> 00:00:06.312
The second is the complete Python reference script.

00:00:06.312 --> 00:00:07.312
The script is useful later when you want to see how all of the separate functions fit together.

00:00:07.312 --> 00:00:07.612
00:00:07.612 --> 00:00:10.422
My recommendation is not to begin by running the complete script and treating it as a black box.

00:00:10.422 --> 00:00:10.722
Follow the smaller steps first.

00:00:10.722 --> 00:00:12.092
Load the data, inspect the chunks, create the embeddings, and test retrieval.

00:00:12.092 --> 00:00:13.737
Then use the complete script as a checkpoint.

00:00:13.737 --> 00:00:15.497
Compare your version with the reference version and make sure you understand why each function exists.

00:00:15.497 --> 00:00:18.252
That workflow is closer to how you should learn a real technical system: first understand the pieces,

00:00:18.252 --> 00:00:18.789
then look at the full implementation.
